    {
      "evidence": "scripts/select_checks.py `drift_base` calls `resolve_changed_file_base`. That function returns None when explicit files are given. `drift_base` then raises SystemExit(\"Explorer editorial drift report needs --base <ref> together with --execute and --changed-file\"). The raise happens before the selector runs. So `scripts/select_checks.py --execute --changed-file X` is rejected, although `template/scripts/select_checks.py` accepts it. The test only asserts the error message for this case.",
      "id": "wrapper-rejects-explicit-changed-file",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The central wrapper does not apply the same base rule as the selector when `--changed-file` is given. The spec says it SHALL resolve the base by the same rule, and `--changed-file` is a valid source of the changed-file set."
    }
